bx is a mixed-license source tree.

bx-owned code
-------------
bx-owned code in this repository is available under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version
("GPL-2.0-or-later"). The full GPLv2 text is included in COPYING.GPL-2.

Imported and upstream-derived code
----------------------------------
Copied or imported code keeps its original license and notices. Known upstream
areas include:

- src/applets/base/bc/ — BSD-2-Clause, plus extra third-party notices in some
  files
- src/applets/network/nc/atomicio.[ch], netcat.[ch], socks.c — OpenBSD/BSD-style
  notices
- src/applets/network/traceroute/ — GPL-2.0-or-later, with clif.[ch] under
  LGPL-2.1-or-later
- src/applets/system/hdparm/ — hdparm BSD-style notice; some files additionally
  allow GPLv2 redistribution
- src/applets/system/screen/ — GNU Screen, GPL-3.0-or-later
- src/applets/text/ed/ — GNU ed, GPL-2.0-or-later
- src/applets/text/edit/vim/ — Vim license
- src/applets/text/edit/runtime/ — curated Vim runtime subset; some files carry
  their own upstream notices
- src/applets/text/jq/upstream/ — jq and bundled upstream components under the
  terms collected in src/applets/text/jq/COPYING.jq
- src/lib/manual/ — mandoc/OpenBSD-derived code under the terms collected in
  src/lib/manual/COPYING.mandoc

Subtree README/COPYING/LICENSE files and per-file headers control when they
differ from this top-level default.

Combined binary note
--------------------
bx is linked as one multicall executable. Because that combined work includes
components under different copyleft terms, the binary you ship must satisfy the
obligations of the included parts. In particular, builds that include the
Screen-derived applet must be distributable under GPL-3.0-or-later-compatible
terms. For that reason the bx-owned default above is GPL-2.0-or-later, not
GPL-2.0-only.
